# Static export (out/) deployed to Hostinger. See docs/deploy/static-export.md.

# Branded 404: Apache serves this file's content for any request that
# doesn't match a real file or directory, while keeping the ORIGINAL
# requested URL in the browser's address bar (this is a local path, not an
# absolute URL, so ErrorDocument substitutes the body only — it does not
# redirect). That lets app/not-found.tsx detect the intended language from
# the URL client-side, and it keeps the real HTTP 404 status: this only
# fires when nothing on disk matches the request, so it never touches an
# existing file, an existing directory, or the root redirect at "/".
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html

# Next's trailingSlash:true output is folders with their own index.html
# (e.g. /ar/about/index.html). Apache's own directory-index + its default
# DirectorySlash redirect (no-slash -> slash) already serve these correctly
# with no rewrite needed; this just makes that explicit rather than relying
# on the host's default.
DirectoryIndex index.html

<IfModule mod_deflate.c>
  AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE text/html text/css application/javascript application/json image/svg+xml
</IfModule>

# Per-directory cache lifetimes (matching next.config.ts's headers() on
# Vercel, which output: 'export' has no server to run) live in fonts/.htaccess
# and videos/.htaccess — <FilesMatch> here would match by filename only, not
# by path, so it can't scope to a subdirectory from the webroot file.
